        hasImage: true,
        body:
            "Copywriting is writing with a specific commercial purpose: to get a reader to take a specific action — click, buy, sign up, call, reply. It is fundamentally different from other kinds of writing because it is judged almost entirely by results, not by how elegant the sentences sound. A copywriter can write a technically flawless paragraph that persuades nobody, and a copywriter can write three blunt, imperfect sentences that sell out a product — the second is the better copy, by the only standard that actually matters in this field.\n\nThis result-first mindset changes how you should approach every piece of writing in this course. Before writing a single word, a professional copywriter asks: who exactly is reading this, what do they currently believe or feel, and what specific action do I need them to take next? Skipping this question and just 'writing something that sounds good' is the single most common reason copy fails to convert.\n\nCopywriting shows up everywhere: product descriptions, social media ads, email subject lines, landing pages, billboards, WhatsApp broadcast messages, even the button text on an app ('Get Started' vs 'Continue' vs 'Claim Your Spot' are different pieces of copy with potentially very different results). By the end of this course, you'll be able to look at any piece of commercial writing and diagnose exactly why it's working or failing to move its reader toward action.",
