      AppLesson(
        title: 'The Welcome Email: First Impressions Matter Most',
        hasImage: true,
        body:
            "The welcome email — sent immediately after someone subscribes to a list — typically has dramatically higher open and engagement rates than almost any other email you'll ever send to that same subscriber, because it arrives at the exact moment of highest interest and freshest attention, right after someone has just actively chosen to opt in. Wasting this high-attention moment on a generic, low-value message is a common and costly mistake.\n\nA strong welcome email does several things efficiently: confirms and reinforces the subscriber's decision to join (reducing any immediate second-guessing or regret), delivers on whatever specific promise convinced them to subscribe in the first place (a free guide, a discount code, access to specific content), and sets clear expectations about what kind of content and how frequently they can expect to hear from you going forward.\n\nMany businesses use the welcome email specifically to invite a small, low-friction action that deepens the relationship immediately — replying to the email with a specific question, following a social account, or browsing a specific starting product category — while attention and goodwill are still at their natural peak, rather than waiting passively for future engagement to happen on its own without any deliberate first nudge.",
